Here’s the update on today's MCP hands-on : 04-09-2026

MCP Client Robustness:

Why we did this

To make the MCP client reliable when the LLM sends invalid requests or when MCP tools fail.

What we implemented
Maximum iteration limit — prevents infinite agent loops.
Tool validation — checks whether the requested tool exists.
Argument validation — checks JSON, required fields, and data types.
Enum validation — allows only valid calculator operations.
MCP error handling — handles tool execution failures such as division by zero.
Tool result handling — handles structured, text, and empty results.
Duplicate-call detection — prevents executing the same tool request repeatedly.
Clean logging — clearly shows LLM and MCP activities.


Tests completed:

Unknown tool → 
Invalid/missing arguments → 
Wrong argument type → 
Invalid enum (power) → 
Division by zero → 
Structured result → 
Text result → 
Empty result → 
